# Close terminals and free ports

Before the final reply, stop processes **you** started in this chat. Closing a terminal pane is not enough; child Node processes can keep the port.

| Service | Port |
|---|---|
| Admin Vite (`admin/`) | **5173** (`strictPort`) |

Free **5173** only when your process, or an orphan from this chat, still holds it.

```powershell
# Only when this chat bound 5173
Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 5173 -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
  Select-Object -ExpandProperty OwningProcess -Unique |
  ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_ -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }
```

```text
❌ BAD — kill whatever is on 5173 because the turn ended
✅ GOOD — leave the user's already-running dev:admin listener alone
```

- Prefer one-shot checks (`npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build` in `admin/`) over a dev server you start.
- Leave a process running only if the user asks.
